y }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}f(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{2t}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-2)t}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-2)t}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=F(s-2),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-2>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeb2589b-0135-5bbb-bc91-ec121ee5defd" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the First Shifting Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f9645ae-d55f-562f-a835-884c71450a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377894} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc64277-6805-5ed2-b0d7-263cf691384a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377895} {:answer/id #uuid "4e9f4243-5c23-5174-bfd5-a7c5030684cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{3t}g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377896} {:answer/id #uuid "39902c0c-d18c-51fc-adfe-1dbe09bffacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{3t}g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebc64277-6805-5ed2-b0d7-263cf691384a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377895} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbc07c37-6856-58c4-8d50-4b1b55c1aae5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 1